# Committed template for `functions/.secret.local` — the emulator-only
# fallback for `defineSecret()`-bound values. The root `postinstall`
# (scripts/ensure-functions-secret-local.mjs) copies this into place whenever
# `.secret.local` is missing, so a fresh checkout or CI runner gets it
# automatically. `.secret.local` itself is gitignored and must stay that way:
# real keys may go in it (see below), so it must be impossible to commit.
#
# Why the emulator needs the file at all: it resolves each declared secret
# from `.secret.local` first and *falls through to a real Google Cloud Secret
# Manager fetch* for any key the file doesn't pin. Measured, not assumed: the
# fetch fires at the first invocation of any function declaring
# `secrets: [...]`, and only errors when the machine has no Google
# credential — on a logged-in machine it succeeds, silently handing the local
# emulator the real production STRIPE_SECRET_KEY. These placeholders exist to
# make that fallthrough unreachable, not to be read: local/CI emulation always
# runs with STRIPE_MOCK_CHECKOUT=true (see .env.demo-trivia-app-e2e +
# src/stripe-client.ts), which never touches them.
#
# Testing locally against a REAL Stripe account through the emulator: put the
# real test-mode keys in `.secret.local` itself — it is gitignored, so they
# cannot end up in a commit. Never put a real value in this template.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder_never_used_in_mock_mode
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder_never_used_in_mock_mode
